{
  "field": "text_case",
  "contract": "apply_text_case (app/agents/_schemas/text_element.py) and applyTextCase (src/apps/web/src/lib/overlay-layout.ts) must produce IDENTICAL strings. The burn dict (build_overlays_from_text_elements) and the CSS preview layout (resolveTextElementsLayout) both carry the transformed text; the stored element keeps the user's casing. KRI-781: Turkish i rules (i<->İ, ı<->I) apply to the whole text when the case's optional top-level `language` is Turkish; otherwise only to whitespace-delimited words that contain a Turkish-only letter (ı İ ğ Ğ ş Ş). Every other word is cased exactly as before, so English naming a Turkish place keeps English i's and word-by-word casing equals whole-text casing. Cases with `language` are helper-only (a stored element carries no language), so the burn-dict/layout halves skip them. KRI-1192: a whitespace-delimited word with a Greek letter upper-cases with the Greek rule (ICU el: accents dropped, a dialytika added where a removed accent kept two vowels apart, the one-letter word ή keeps its accent); title case keeps the initial's accent.",
  "asserted_by": [
    "src/apps/api/tests/pipeline/test_text_element_parity_contract.py",
    "src/apps/web/src/__tests__/lib/text-element-parity-contract.test.ts"
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "upper",
      "element": {
        "id": "tc-upper",
        "text": "hello World",
        "start_s": 0.0,
        "end_s": 2.0,
        "size_px": 72,
        "text_case": "upper"
      },
      "expected": { "text": "HELLO WORLD" }
    },
    {
      "name": "lower",
      "element": {
        "id": "tc-lower",
        "text": "HELLO World",
        "start_s": 0.0,
        "end_s": 2.0,
